' ============================================================
' Simple Slice Test
' ============================================================
'
' WHAT THIS FILE TEACHES:
'   - []STRING: how to declare a "slice" (a dynamic list/array)
'     A slice is like a list that can grow or shrink as needed.
'     Unlike a fixed-size array, you don't have to say how many
'     items it will hold up front.
'
' NOTE: This file just declares a slice. In a full program,
' you would add items to it with APPEND and loop through it
' with FOR EACH or a regular FOR loop.
' ============================================================

' Declare a slice (dynamic list) of strings.
' Right now it's empty -- it has zero items in it.
' You could add items like: names = APPEND(names, "Alice")
DIM names AS []STRING
